From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi-cir: keep receiving in suspend as a wakeup source

sunxi-cir gates its clocks and asserts reset on suspend, so a remote can
never wake the system. Stock H713 firmware wakes from the remote's power key,
and the projector's standby (s2idle, there being no PSCI SYSTEM_SUSPEND)
needs the same.

Honour the standard wakeup-source property: register the device as wakeup
capable, and when wakeup is enabled leave the receiver running across
suspend and arm its interrupt as a wake interrupt instead of shutting it
down. Without the property nothing changes.

The decoder runs on the CPU, so in s2idle any IR frame wakes the system,
not only the power key; the standby daemon decides what to do once awake.
Mark the bench board's receiver wakeup-source.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 
 &r_ir {
 	linux,rc-map-name = "rc-hy200-projector";
+	wakeup-source;
 };
 
 &ppu {
--- a/drivers/media/rc/sunxi-cir.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/sunxi-cir.c
@@ -266,6 +266,12 @@
 
 static int __maybe_unused sunxi_ir_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
+	struct sunxi_ir *ir = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/* A wakeup source keeps receiving, so a key press can wake us. */
+	if (device_may_wakeup(dev))
+		return enable_irq_wake(ir->irq);
+
 	sunxi_ir_hw_exit(dev);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -273,6 +279,11 @@
 
 static int __maybe_unused sunxi_ir_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
+	struct sunxi_ir *ir = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (device_may_wakeup(dev))
+		return disable_irq_wake(ir->irq);
+
 	return sunxi_ir_hw_init(dev);
 }
 
@@ -393,6 +404,8 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto exit_free_dev;
 
+	device_init_wakeup(dev, of_property_read_bool(dn, "wakeup-source"));
+
 	dev_info(dev, "initialized sunXi IR driver\n");
 
 	return 0;
